On 10/08/2017 08:07, vpbroman@gmail.com wrote:
> When you say "you can express all that Lojban can express with a very=20
> limited set of cmavo", does that mean someone has already done such a=20
> reduction and arrived at a small/minimal set of cmavo that is sufficient?
>

Here's a quick list of what seems to me to be a pretty minimal set of=20
cmavo (maybe I'm forgetting some important ones, so don't take it as=20
definitive):

=E2=80=A2 co'e
=E2=80=A2 [be, bei, be'o] / [poi'i, ke'a, kei]
=E2=80=A2 [[lo/su'o/ro/no], du'u, ka, ce'u, kei, cu] / [ko'ai, xu'u, ku'au,=
 ko'V]
=E2=80=A2 xi, PA

MAYBE: .i, ca'e
EXTRALOGICAL: kau (as a focus marker)

The '/' signifies alternative possibilities.

Connectives and other quantifiers would be expressed with predicates and=20
nested abstractions.

=E2=80=94Ilmen.


